    "source": "// 水滴レンズ / SUITEKI — UNFOLD IMAGE SURFACE function body.\n// Surface only: workshop「立体化なし」 / 1 image「立体化する」OFF /\n// sequence「形にしない」. A/B and their alpha remain host-owned.\n// Optional numeric params use the suiteki... names below.\nconst DROPLETS = 24;       // 6–32\nconst RADIUS = 1.0;        // 0.45–1.5 : droplet size\nconst REFRACTION = 0.82;   // 0–1.2 : actual source-image lensing\nconst SPEED = 0.58;        // 0–2 : breathing / slow downward drift\nconst GLINT = 0.26;        // 0–0.65 : wet specular / Fresnel edge\nconst FILM = 0.12;         // 0–0.5 : very light continuous water film\nconst SEED = 17;           // 0–1000 : static deterministic placement\nconst clamp = (value, lo, hi) => Math.min(hi, Math.max(lo, value));\nconst number = (value, fallback, lo, hi) => clamp(Number.isFinite(value) ? value : fallback, lo, hi);\nconst ease = value => { const x = clamp(value, 0, 1); return x * x * (3 - 2 * x); };\nconst params = api.params || {};\nconst plane = api.createImagePlane();\nconst material = plane.material;\nconst imageWidth = number(api.size && api.size.width, 1, 0.001, 10000);\nconst imageHeight = number(api.size && api.size.height, 1, 0.001, 10000);\nconst uniforms = material.uniforms;\nuniforms.uSuitekiAspect = { value: clamp(imageWidth / imageHeight, 0.1, 10) };\nuniforms.uSuitekiAmount = { value: 0 };\nuniforms.uSuitekiTime = { value: 0 };\nuniforms.uSuitekiPixel = { value: 1 / 900 };\nuniforms.uSuitekiCount = { value: Math.round(number(params.suitekiCount, DROPLETS, 6, 32)) };\nuniforms.uSuitekiRadius = { value: number(params.suitekiRadius, RADIUS, 0.45, 1.5) };\nuniforms.uSuitekiRefraction = { value: number(params.suitekiRefraction, REFRACTION, 0, 1.2) };\nuniforms.uSuitekiSpeed = { value: number(params.suitekiSpeed, SPEED, 0, 2) };\nuniforms.uSuitekiGlint = { value: number(params.suitekiGlint, GLINT, 0, 0.65) };\nuniforms.uSuitekiFilm = { value: number(params.suitekiFilm, FILM, 0, 0.5) };\nuniforms.uSuitekiSeed = { value: number(params.suitekiSeed, SEED, 0, 1000) };\n\n// Keep createImagePlane's material and a/b/mixImage uniform objects intact.\n// This shader is for that image plane only; never copy it to a 3D material.\nmaterial.fragmentShader = `\nuniform sampler2D a, b;\nuniform float mixImage;\nvarying vec2 vUv;\nuniform float uSuitekiAspect;\nuniform float uSuitekiAmount;\nuniform float uSuitekiTime;\nuniform float uSuitekiPixel;\nuniform float uSuitekiCount;\nuniform float uSuitekiRadius;\nuniform float uSuitekiRefraction;\nuniform float uSuitekiSpeed;\nuniform float uSuitekiGlint;\nuniform float uSuitekiFilm;\nuniform float uSuitekiSeed;\n\nvec2 suitekiOffset;\nfloat suitekiCoverage;\nfloat suitekiLight;\nfloat suitekiShade;\n\nfloat suitekiHash(float n) {\n  return fract(sin(n * 127.1 + uSuitekiSeed * 31.73) * 43758.5453);\n}\n\nvoid suitekiSurface(vec2 uv) {\n  vec2 metric = vec2(uSuitekiAspect, 1.0);\n  vec2 p = (uv - 0.5) * metric;\n  float t = uSuitekiTime * uSuitekiSpeed;\n  float columns = clamp(floor(sqrt(uSuitekiCount * uSuitekiAspect)), 1.0, 16.0);\n  float rows = ceil(uSuitekiCount / columns);\n  vec2 cell = metric / vec2(columns, rows);\n  float cellMin = min(cell.x, cell.y);\n  float strongest = 0.0;\n  suitekiOffset = vec2(0.0);\n  suitekiCoverage = 0.0;\n  suitekiLight = 0.0;\n  suitekiShade = 0.0;\n\n  // One fixed-bounded shader loop, no particles or extra meshes.\n  for (int i = 0; i < 32; i++) {\n    float id = float(i);\n    if (id >= uSuitekiCount) break;\n    float h0 = suitekiHash(id + 1.7);\n    float h1 = suitekiHash(id + 13.2);\n    float h2 = suitekiHash(id + 38.9);\n    float h3 = suitekiHash(id + 75.4);\n    float phase = h2 * 6.2831853;\n    vec2 grid = vec2(mod(id, columns), floor(id / columns));\n    vec2 center = (grid + 0.5) * cell - 0.5 * metric;\n    center += (vec2(h0, h1) - 0.5) * cell * 0.43;\n    // Bounded slow slide and breathing, computed from the requested time.\n    center.x += sin(t * 0.37 + phase) * cell.x * 0.065;\n    center.y += sin(t * 0.24 + phase * 1.7) * cell.y * 0.105;\n    float breath = 1.0 + 0.07 * sin(t * 0.69 + phase);\n    float radius = cellMin * mix(0.265, 0.45, h3) * uSuitekiRadius * breath;\n    radius *= mix(0.83, 1.0, uSuitekiAmount);\n    vec2 oval = vec2(mix(0.83, 1.08, h1), mix(0.95, 1.15, h0));\n    float angle = (h2 - 0.5) * 0.9;\n    float cs = cos(angle), sn = sin(angle);\n    mat2 rotation = mat2(cs, -sn, sn, cs);\n    vec2 delta = p - center;\n    vec2 local = rotation * delta / (radius * oval);\n    // A slight hanging pear shape distinguishes water from glass marbles.\n    local.x *= 1.0 + 0.09 * clamp(local.y, -1.0, 1.0);\n    float radial = length(local);\n    float feather = clamp(uSuitekiPixel * 1.4 / radius, 0.012, 0.085);\n    float coverage = 1.0 - smoothstep(1.0 - feather, 1.0 + feather, radial);\n    if (coverage <= 0.0) continue;\n    float r2 = min(radial * radial, 1.0);\n    float cap = sqrt(max(0.0, 1.0 - r2));\n    float rank = coverage * (cap + 0.018);\n\n    // The dominant rounded cap wins in overlaps, avoiding additive UV spikes.\n    if (rank > strongest) {\n      strongest = rank;\n      float rim = pow(r2, 4.0);\n      float magnify = -0.67 * cap + 0.28 * rim;\n      suitekiOffset = delta / metric * magnify * uSuitekiRefraction;\n      suitekiCoverage = coverage;\n      vec3 normal = normalize(vec3(local * 0.92, max(0.06, cap)));\n      vec3 halfLight = normalize(vec3(-0.26, 0.38, 1.8));\n      float specular = pow(max(dot(normal, halfLight), 0.0), 72.0);\n      float fresnel = pow(1.0 - cap, 3.0);\n      float upperArc = pow(max(dot(normal.xy, normalize(vec2(-0.65, 0.76))), 0.0), 7.0);\n      float lowerArc = pow(max(dot(normal.xy, normalize(vec2(0.38, -0.92))), 0.0), 10.0);\n      suitekiLight = coverage * (specular * 0.9 + fresnel * (0.32 * upperArc + 0.1 * lowerArc));\n      suitekiShade = coverage * fresnel * 0.19;\n    }\n  }\n  // Barely visible interstitial water, also actual source UV displacement.\n  vec2 filmFlow = vec2(\n    sin(p.y * 18.0 + t * 0.33) * cos(p.x * 8.0 - t * 0.17),\n    sin(p.x * 13.0 - t * 0.22) * cos(p.y * 9.0 + t * 0.14)\n  );\n  suitekiOffset += filmFlow / metric * uSuitekiFilm * 0.006 * (1.0 - suitekiCoverage);\n}\n\nvec4 suitekiSample(sampler2D source, vec2 uv) {\n  vec4 original = texture2D(source, uv);\n  if (uSuitekiAmount <= 0.0) return original;\n  vec2 refractedUV = clamp(uv + suitekiOffset * uSuitekiAmount, vec2(0.001), vec2(0.999));\n  vec4 refracted = texture2D(source, refractedUV);\n  float wet = max(suitekiCoverage, uSuitekiFilm) * uSuitekiAmount;\n  // Original straight alpha is exact. Transparent sampled pixels cannot\n  // introduce black fringes or turn the transparent exterior into a lens.\n  float sourceWeight = wet * clamp(refracted.a, 0.0, 1.0);\n  vec3 color = mix(original.rgb, refracted.rgb, sourceWeight);\n  return vec4(color, original.a);\n}\n\nvoid main() {\n  suitekiOffset = vec2(0.0);\n  suitekiCoverage = 0.0;\n  suitekiLight = 0.0;\n  suitekiShade = 0.0;\n  if (uSuitekiAmount > 0.0) suitekiSurface(vUv);\n  vec4 tex = mix(suitekiSample(a, vUv), suitekiSample(b, vUv), mixImage);\n  if (uSuitekiAmount > 0.0) {\n    float visible = step(0.00001, tex.a);\n    tex.rgb *= 1.0 - suitekiShade * uSuitekiAmount;\n    tex.rgb += vec3(0.94, 0.98, 1.0) * suitekiLight * uSuitekiGlint * uSuitekiAmount * visible;\n  }\n  gl_FragColor = tex;\n  #include <colorspace_fragment>\n}\n`;\nmaterial.needsUpdate = true;\n\nreturn {\n  physicsTime: () => 0,\n  update(frame) {\n    const duration = number(frame.duration, 1, 0.001, 86400);\n    const time = number(frame.clipTime, 0, 0, 86400);\n    const progress = number(frame.progress, time / duration, 0, 1);\n    const amount = number(frame.amount, 0, 0, 1);\n    const envelope = ease(progress / 0.13) * ease((1 - progress) / 0.18);\n    uniforms.uSuitekiTime.value = time;\n    uniforms.uSuitekiAmount.value = clamp(amount / 0.8, 0, 1) * envelope;\n    uniforms.uSuitekiPixel.value = 1 / number(frame.height, 900, 16, 16384);\n  }\n};\n",
